= Overview
In requirements-specifications of #ref(<prestudy>) the requirements for the solution were defined. In this chapter the requirements are verified against the implemented solution to ensure that all requirements are properly met. The verification is done by testing the implemented solution against the requirements and documenting the results. The requirements are divided into functional and non-functional requirements, and each requirement is verified separately.

